{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778123126,"nonce":"XbI3iST1N1V0ce2FokNazPVg00o=","message":"## Design decisions surfaced during rlrmp's CLAUDE.md \\`## Issue Coordination\\` write-up\n\nWhen the comprehensive Issue Coordination section was drafted (rlrmp \\`bcb2205\\`, merged via \\`51621ad1\\`), several judgment calls came up that the templating mechanism should consider as defaults or configurable knobs:\n\n1. **Wording strength** — \"should be minimal\" vs \"must be minimal\" for the umbrella-verbosity directive. Templates likely want \"must\" for project-internal CLAUDE.md to make rules unambiguous.\n\n2. **Worked example** — every coord-protocol section benefits from one concrete example. Templates should slot one in (or have a placeholder + suggestion to fill in from project specifics).\n\n3. **Anticipating future axes** — rlrmp's CLAUDE.md anticipates a future model-structure coord with a row in the decision-flow table. Templates should be configurable to either include such anticipations or stay minimal.\n\n4. **Phase umbrella auto-close behavior** — design choice: when a child commit references the umbrella in \\`Bug:\\` trailer, the umbrella auto-closes (matches \\`b557d4e\\` precedent) and the comment thread carries the phase state. Templates could parameterize this — some phases want to stay open as living docs.\n\n5. **Label-discipline section** — global CLAUDE.md covers feature/error labels. Project-level CLAUDE.md doesn't restate. Templates should default to NOT restating, but allow optional rlrmp-style \"use these labels\" enforcement when desired.\n\nThese are decision points — the templating feature should encode them as defaults or knobs when generalizing.","files":null}]}